      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Including very poor as an option for quest without other thought would just make it so that quest users don't get any of the benefit of the feature. If they had a polygon limit when selecting very poor for quest it would still have a point. I'd suggest something like 36k or 70k. \n\nInterestingly enough, Ready Player Me avatars were actually available in different quality levels, so I actually have an avatar that is rated good on both PC and quest. The PC avatar definately has more polygons than the quest version. \n\nMost users that saved a model file from rpm have the PC version, so it's Good on PC, and medium on quest.\n\nWay off topic but if I could download my imposter and replace the hands, I'd do exactly that for quest and iOS",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-05-22T04:38:07.644Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Performance gating is a really good feature, the problem is that it only allows you to set the limits the same across all platforms, even though the performance ranks are vastly different between Windows and Android/iOS. A Good or Medium rank avatar on PC can and will often be Very Poor on quest. This creates an issue where users in performance-gated instances will be driven to use PC-only avatars. This feature excludes quest users and groups who want to accommodate Quest users. Please allow different performance limits to pe chosen for each platform-including Very Poor for Android and iOS.",
